spended the dollar’s conversion into gold for foreign official holders, undermining the Bretton Woods monetary system.","format":"context_relation","references":[{"file":"Original · general culture extension","verificationUrl":"https://www.imf.org/external/about/timeline/index.htm","checkedOnline93":true}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v93","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"context_relation","topic74":"What did the United States suspend during the Nixon shock?","difficulty74":"unrated","testedFactKeys":["original93|what did the united states suspend during the nixon shock|dollar convertibility into gold"],"reviewStatus":"editorial-reviewed","lineage74":"Original study question; not an official exam item.","evidence":{"type":"editorial-source-review","checkedAt":"2026-10-07","review":"Primary/institutional reference checked; concise distractors reviewed; screened against active Alpha and original questions."},"fingerprint":"4ad1032b42c33c677c44"},{"id":"ARCHED-B100-20261007-001","qid":950001,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B100-20261007-001","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B100-20261007-001"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"Architecture","group":"Pont du Gard","stem":"Roman aqueducts normally carried water by:","choices":["Siphon pumps","Water screws","Gravity","Bucket chains","Piston pumps"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":"Gravity","explanation":"A slight downward gradient lets gravity move the water. Bridges keep the channel at the required elevation.","format":"single_best_answer","references":[{"file":"UNESCO — Pont du Gard (Roman Aqueduct)","verificationUrl":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/344/","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"A01","title":"UNESCO — Pont du Gard (Roman Aqueduct)","url":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/344/","verification_status":"reference_supplied; see retrieval report","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"previous_batch_inherited"}},{"file":"V100 institutional reference check","verificationUrl":"https://pontdugard.fr/en/discover/monument","checkedAt":"2026-10-09","supportScope":"Gravity flow along a small gradient"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":1,"canonical_number":null,"revision95":2,"topic74":"Pont du Gard","skill74":"context_relation","testedRelation95":"B100:pont-du-gard","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["TOPIC:pont-du-gard"],"workIds95":[],"evidenceStatus95":"reference_only_pending_external_check","exactDuplicateOf95":[],"sourceSnapshotHash95":"c5b5a1e1b67276058524d71a1baf8d12c78db22b6e69c82d67e29ed146c0facb","fingerprint":"f42dc4e407ca46665a19","review100":{"date":"2026-10-09","scope":"Stem, five alternatives, correct answer and explanation reviewed. Retained source provenance is not an assertion of fresh external verification.","sourceVerification":"reference_only_pending_external_check","decision":"revised_and_adopted"}},{"id":"ARCHED-B100-20261007-003","qid":950003,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B100-20261007-003","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B100-20261007-003"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"Architecture","group":"Pendentive","stem":"What problem does a pendentive solve in a domed building?","choices":["Supporting a circular dome above a square space","Providing a horizontal lintel above a doorway","Closing the opening at the top of a dome","Dividing a long nave into side aisles","Joining two flat roofs at different heights"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":"Supporting a circular dome above a square space","explanation":"A pendentive is a curved, triangular transition between a square bay and the circular base of a dome. It is not the small opening at the dome’s crown.","format":"single_best_answer","references":[{"file":"Smarthistory — Hagia Sophia, Istanbul","verificationUrl":"https://smarthistory.org/hagia-sophia-istanbul/","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"A03","title":"Smarthistory — Hagi