pporting the principal altar","An underground chamber used only for royal burials","A projecting bay for the main church organ","A tower containing the monastery bells"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":"Covered circulation around an open courtyard","explanation":"A cloister links covered walks around a court with adjacent monastic buildings. It is both a spatial arrangement and a circulation system, not the courtyard alone.","format":"context_relation","references":[{"file":"Encyclopaedia reference — Cloister","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloister","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B03-S-Cloister","key":"Cloister","title":"Encyclopaedia reference — Cloister","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloister","source_type":"tertiary_encyclopaedia","verification_status":"reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","checked_at":null,"support_scope":"Reference supplied for this topic; no claim that its live text was read in this pass.","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"reference_only"}}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":121,"canonical_number":null,"revision95":2,"topic74":"Cloister and monastic circulation","skill74":"context_relation","testedRelation95":"B02R2:cloister-and-monastic-circulation","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["TOPIC:cloister-and-monastic-circulation"],"workIds95":[],"evidenceStatus95":"reference_only_pending_external_check","exactDuplicateOf95":[],"sourceSnapshotHash95":"8c60e4338bfd989c7498969e1d8a43fa7daf0b2a3322436cb44d51675a1034f3","fingerprint":"e5cae7cb4da3a75ccd4b","review100":{"date":"2026-10-09","scope":"Stem, five alternatives, correct answer and explanation reviewed. Retained source provenance is not an assertion of fresh external verification.","sourceVerification":"reference_only_pending_external_check","decision":"adopted"}},{"id":"ARCHED-B02-20261007-122","qid":950122,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B02-20261007-122","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B02-20261007-122"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"Architecture","group":"Minaret function","stem":"A minaret is traditionally associated with which activity?","choices":["Indicating the direction of prayer through an interior niche","Housing the main pulpit from which a sermon is delivered","Calling the faithful to prayer","Marking the tomb chamber beneath a mosque","Providing the basin for ritual washing"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":"Calling the faithful to prayer","explanation":"A minaret is a tower associated with a mosque. It differs from the mihrab, which is the prayer-direction niche inside the mosque.","format":"single_best_answer","references":[{"file":"Merriam-Webster — minaret","verificationUrl":"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/minaret","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B02-A22","title":"Merriam-Webster — minaret","url":"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/minaret","support_summary":"A minaret is a tower associated with a mosque and traditionally used for the call to prayer.","verification_status":"supporting_web_text_read","checked_on":"2026-10-07","verification_method":"Author read the cited supporting web text; not independent expert certification.","source_type":"editorial_dictionary","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"previous_batch_inherited"}}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":122,"canonical_number":null,"revision95":1,"topic74":"Minaret function","skill74":"context_relation","testedRelation95":"B02:minaret-function","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["TOPIC:minaret-function"],"workIds95":[],"evidenceStatus95":"supporting_text_records_available","exactDuplicateOf95":[],"sourceSnapshotHash95":"b945bc3a4b7206427fb497a6093882ab994398c65fbd943bbe826f1cd6f487aa","finge